{"name":"Yoshi","hex":"#55aa00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Yoshi","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from Japanese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Yoshi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yoshi","blocks":[{"text":"T. Yoshisaur Munchakoopas, commonly known as Yoshi is a fictional character who appears in video games published by Nintendo. He was designed by Shigefumi Hino and first appeared in Super Mario World (1990) for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System as a rideable companion for Mario and Luigi. The character belongs to a species of dinosaur-like creatures, also called Yoshis, which are commonly depicted in different colors and are known for using their long tongues to eat enemies and produce eggs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/db/Yoshi_%28Nintendo_character%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi","wikidata":"Q214174"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Yoshi-concept.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Yoshi-concept.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Considered after the development of Super Mario Bros., Yoshi's early design differs greatly from his finished appearance.[13]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoshi-concept.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/Super_Mario_World.png/250px-Super_Mario_World.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Super_Mario_World.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/14/Super_Mario_World.png/250px-Super_Mario_World.png?ut